[4407138952] Upstream Reporter: Yaakov Selkowitz
Upstream issue status: Open
Upstream description: {quote}Reported by @hroncok in chat:

{quote}
python-inotify was in ELN. Now it was retired in favor of python-pyinotify. Same upstream, packaged under more correct name. It now pulls in pyasyncore unconditionally - the older package had a patch that moved the import away from global scope. Anyway, upstream pyinotify is dead either way.

[https://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms/python-inotify/c/7db1b34f7d4799c99215afc912625b637caea4d0?branch=rawhide] [https://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms/python-inotify/blob/f7/f/python-inotify.spec] [https://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms/python-pyinotify/c/dd09347f6569b1850ce572abde1d664e2651fa43?branch=rawhide]
{quote}
The aforementioned patch was restored in [https://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms/python-pyinotify/c/e8952a90e4758a1ae6ed88d783088e39a307d082?branch=rawhide], so this is now a simple rename.
{quote}
Upstream URL: https://github.com/fedora-eln/eln/issues/514

